# Everything a run produces. These are outputs, not sources: the warrant ids
# change on every run, and committing them would make each demo a diff.
*.tex
*.pdf
*.aux
*.log
*.out

# Every JSON a build script drops beside itself — warrants, refusals,
# generations, monitoring records. This started as a list of names and grew one
# at a time as each new case study wrote a new one, which meant three separate
# commits each had a generated file in it. No case study has a hand-written
# JSON source, so the rule is the shape: any JSON in a case-study folder is
# output. Add `!thefile.json` if that ever stops being true.
*/*.json

# The Ames data is third-party and downloaded on first run. It belongs to its
# publisher, it is a megabyte, and the script fetches it from the authoritative
# URL — a copy in here would be exactly the convenient mirror the README argues
# against.
02_home_price_regression/data/

# The trained artifact. Case study 13 exports an ONNX graph, and the whole
# point of that case study is that the bytes are the model — so a copy checked
# in here would be a second model with no training run behind it, going stale
# the first time anybody changes a hyperparameter. It is 756 bytes and it
# regenerates in under a minute.
*.onnx
